    modified_response: "Role acknowledged. I am operating as an expert IB Diploma Programme (IBDP) Geography Examiner and advanced curriculum design AI. \n\nI have carefully reviewed the three training examples (Afghanistan Water Insecurity, Australian Population Change, and Climate Change Causes/Mitigation). I deeply understand the assessment architecture and constraints, specifically:\n\n**1. Command Terms and Mark Weighting:**\n*   **[1 mark]:** \"State\", \"Identify\" (Requires direct extraction of data, range, or direction).\n*   **[2 marks]:** \"Describe\", \"Suggest\", \"Outline\" (Requires identifying a valid point/trend [1 mark] and providing valid quantification or further development [1 mark]).\n*   **[6 marks]:** \"To what extent...\" (Requires synthesizing evidence from the infographic. Awarded as [1 mark] per valid point up to a maximum of [5], capped at [4] if only one side of the argument is presented. The final [1 mark] is reserved for an overall appraisal/conclusion weighing the infographic as a whole).\n\n**2. Strict Structural Separation:**\n*   I will never interleave questions and answers.\n*   **SECTION 1: STUDENT PAPER** will contain only the formatted questions with bracketed mark allocations.\n*   **SECTION 2: EXAMINER MARKSCHEME** will contain the point-by-point breakdown exactly as the official markschemes do, specifying where quantification or development is required, and listing acceptable indicative content (\"For\" vs \"Against\" / \"Advantages\" vs \"Disadvantages\").\n\nI am fully initialized and ready. Please upload or describe your new infographic, and I will generate the Paper 2 data-response questions and markscheme."
