ling. The header will be updated to display \"Infographic Generator\". I will also convert the accents to green by changing `bg-indigo-600` elements to `bg-emerald-500` to maintain consistency throughout.\n\nI\'ve re-evaluated the green and decided to keep it simple, opting for `emerald-500` for the logo\'s background for now. This will allow for easier palette consistency. I\'m now replacing all `indigo` color references in the code with `emerald`, keeping things straightforward. I will also make the logo a rounded square with `rounded-2xl`, with a green background and bold, white \"DP\". I will now review the target `App.tsx` file.\n\nI\'m now focusing on specific visual elements within the code, such as the rounded indigo backgrounds and text colors. I will update these to match the agreed-upon green accent throughout the components. I will ensure that the changes are visually consistent and harmonious with the updated logo and title. I need to keep in mind other components that might rely on these visual elements.\n\nI\'m now revising the border styles. I\'m swapping the custom shadow for a more standard Tailwind approach, evaluating `ring-4 ring-emerald-500/20` versus `border-4 border-emerald-50`. To achieve the precise logo ring, I\'ll consider using a custom hex code for the background, but will keep the Tailwind class for the time being. I\'ll test the effects of the border, but am leaning toward simplifying.\n```\n\n**Refining Code Updates**\n\nI\'m now implementing targeted code changes. The logo\'s initial `div` in `App.tsx` is updated. I\'ve switched from a custom shadow to Tailwind\'s classes: `bg-emerald-500 rounded-xl` to make it a green rounded square with white \"DP\". The title is now \"Infographic Generator\". I also have a list of all `indigo` references that are targets for global replacement by `emerald`. I\'ll next update the sidebar styles to reflect this. I have prepared the chunks for `multi_edit_file` to perform this, including the header 