  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Refining Question Generation**\n\nI\'m now focusing on refining the prompt for Gemini. My goal is to ensure the generated questions consistently adhere to the specified IB marking style. I\'m prioritizing the Part (a) structure - either 1-1-2 or a single 2-mark question, followed by a Part (b) question, and a distinct Part (c). This is a crucial step towards aligning the output with the IB assessment framework.\n\n\n**Structuring Question Parts**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the structure of the 6-marker questions to ensure they encompass balance and evaluation. I\'ve analyzed sample IB questions, which are essential for aligning my prompt with the IB assessment framework. I need to generate Part (c) questions that will be effective 6-marker questions. This will include an introductory statement.\n\n\n**Enforcing Question Structure**\n\nI\'m now revising my prompt to rigidly enforce the IB question structure: a 2-mark Part (a), a 2-mark Part (b) (suggest/outline, synthesis/reasoning), and a 6-mark Part (c) asking, \"To what extent does the evidence support...\". This refinement ensures the AI-generated questions conform to the standard IB assessment format, so that the assessment will be as accurate as possible.\n\n\n**Formalizing IB Questions**\n\nI\'m now drafting questions that mirror IBDP Geography Paper 2\'s style, tone, and difficulty. The focus is on creating questions with a specific structure. The prompts will have three main questions with precisely defined parts. This includes a clear markscheme for each question, mirroring the strict assessment criteria. It will provide a detailed breakdown, including \"For\" and \"Against\" sections for the 6-mark questions.\n\n\n**Defining JSON Structure**\n\nI am now focusing on the strict JSON output format. I\'m ensuring the \'marks\' field accepts numbers, which means I will rewrite prompts so that if Question (a) has sub-questions, they can be listed in the text, and their marks are tallied in the \'marks\' field. I am also working on the structure, specifically \'criteria\' and \'paths\' under the markscheme to include a detailed breakdown, including \"For\" and \"Against\" sections for the 6-mark questions.\n\n\n"
