    thinking: "**Refining the Prompt**\n\nI\'ve decided to hardcode the prompt string directly within `server.ts`. This ensures precise adherence to the desired structure by removing any flexibility for deviation.\n\n\n**Defining the Task**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the core objective: generating data-response questions and markschemes. The goal is to accurately analyze infographics for geographical content and produce questions that mirror the style and rigor of the IBDP Geography Paper 2. I\'m prioritizing the strict question structure, ensuring exactly three questions are generated per prompt, worth a total of ten marks.\n\n\n**Structuring the Responses**\n\nI\'m now meticulously crafting the required markscheme format. The goal is pinpoint accuracy, to match the IBDP style. I\'m focusing on providing point-by-point breakdowns for parts (a) and (b), with clear mark allocation. For part (c), I\'ll definitely integrate a \"Supportive\" and \"Counter/Non-supportive\" section, following the IBDP criteria precisely.\n\n\n**Clarifying Mark Allocation**\n\nI\'m now refining the specification for mark allocation to avoid redundancy. I\'ll ensure the `text` field provides only the descriptive content, excluding explicit mark indications, which will be handled elsewhere, but still contain the format \"(a) (i) State ... \\\\n(ii) State ...\". The `paths` array will contain comprehensive details, including point-by-point mark distribution, to ensure the frontend can render mark schemes accurately. The goal is to avoid repeating the mark values, which the front end will render as \"\\[X marks] (text)\". Also, I\'m thinking of how to display the loading state during generation, with a spinner.\n\n\n**Adjusting Frontend Display**\n\nI\'m now integrating `whitespace-pre-wrap` into the front-end to handle newline characters in question text from the markscheme. This ensures multi-line questions, such as those with parts (a)(i) and (ii), display correctly. Previously, these newlines were not rendering properly; this is now fixed!\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 13
      nanos: 764798379
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
