  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Assessing the Logo Update**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the logo. I\'ve broken down the request, and the key element is matching the Examiner App\'s rounded square logo. I\'m focusing on the green color, which seems to be close to #00a672, but requires some fine-tuning based on the visual. Right now, I am estimating the color from the image.\n\n\n**Refining the Color Palette**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on the color palette for the logo. The initial green, which I was estimating from the image, now has a specific, bright green hex value to work with: `#09bc73`. I\'m confident about incorporating this shade, and will likely also explore its darker variations for dark mode implementation. Now I am focused on the \"DP\" text, and the font is likely sans-serif.\n\n\n**Implementing the Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m now implementing the dark mode toggle. I\'m focusing on the `isDarkMode` state and the associated `dark` class applied to the root element. I\'m aiming for the dark mode to seamlessly change the color palette of the application, and am incorporating the bright green hex value `#00c473` as the primary color. Next, I am thinking about the title structure and font choices, and considering the use of different font weights for visual hierarchy. I am focused on creating a font-weight contrast for visual appeal.\n\n\n**Configuring the Dark Mode**\n\nI\'m now integrating dark mode configurations directly within `index.css` using standard `dark:` utility classes. My approach involves wrapping the main `App.tsx` div with a conditional class, applying the `dark` class based on the `isDarkMode` state. Inside, the app background will now toggle between `bg-slate-50` and `dark:bg-slate-900`. I\'m also implementing a dark mode toggle button in the header with a Moon/Sun icon. I am updating the header logo with `bg-[#00c473]`.\nI am also updating all `bg-white` to `bg-white dark:bg-slate-800`, text colors to `text-slate-900 dark:text-white`, and borders to `border-slate-200 dark:border-slate-700`.\n\n\n**Adjusting Visual Elements**\n\nI\'m now adjusting the muted text to `text-slate-500 dark:text-slate-400` and secondary backgrounds to `bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-900`. I am updating the accent borders, and updating the Generate button\'s color. Next, I\'m focusing on the font and matching it to that of my Examiner App, like Poppins or Montserrat. I\'ve added Google Font `Poppins` to `index.css`. I\'ve updated Tailwind CSS variables.\nI\'ve checked Vite v4 Tailwind Dark Mode and I\'m updating it via configuration.\n\n\n\n**Revising Dark Mode Strategy**\n\nI\'m now revising my dark mode strategy for Tailwind v4. It appears the `dark:` utility class is the standard and correct approach. I\'m focusing on ensuring its proper implementation, updating colors to the desired `#1e2329`, and testing for visual consistency. I\'m replacing `bg-white` with `bg-white dark:bg-[#1e2329]`.\n\n\n**Refining Color and Text**\n\nI\'m now refining the color and text, and updating the overall theme. I am transitioning from `bg-slate-900` to a new shade of dark gray, `#1e2329`. I\'ve updated the background from `bg-slate-50` to `bg-slate-50 dark:bg-slate-950`, and text colors using a comprehensive range of updates, such as updating `text-slate-900` to `text-slate-900 dark:text-slate-100`, for contrast in dark mode. Border colors are also modified for the overall visual harmony. I am also planning on modifying the App Title.\n\n\n**Updating the UI Elements**\n\nI\'m now updating the UI elements, refining the look and feel. I am focusing on revising the title structure, and plan on updating the title with a bold font and appropriate spacing. I\'m also updating the header components, and I will be using `bg-[#00c473]` for all accent colors. Also, I am updating the dark mode toggle button to a more visually appealing design. Finally, I will be updating the \"accent green\" to match the examiner app.\n\n\n\n**Implementing the Color Scheme**\n\nI\'m now implementing an emerald color scheme, and adjusting border and text classes for dark mode. I am updating the color scheme to enhance the user interface, incorporating emerald tones and ensuring a coherent visual experience in both light and dark modes. I\'m focusing on ensuring consistency across all elements. Also, I am revising the title structure. I\'m focusing on the font and checking the `index.css` for any changes.\n\n\n**Revising Dark Mode Config**\n\nI\'m now revising the dark mode configuration. I\'ve re-examined Tailwind v4\'s dark mode handling and I\'m updating `src/index.css`. I am focusing on using class-based dark mode natively by setting the selector with the theme config. I am checking the `index.css` file to see the `@custom-variant dark (&:is(.dark *));` to implement the `dark:` utility class. I am also making sure that `--font-sans` setting is working.\n\n\n**Finalizing Title and Elements**\n\nI\'m now finalizing the title and other header elements for the interface. I\'ve updated the background color to align with the chosen dark mode colors. The container is now using a combination of classes, including the dark mode variants. The logo now displays the appropriate background color in both light and dark modes. I\'m focusing on the overall layout, making sure that it looks aesthetically appealing and the content is well-aligned. The title uses a bold, black font to show the text, and displays \"DP\" in black color.\n\n\n**Adjusting Active State**\n\nI\'m now focusing on the active state indicators. I am updating the current active status indicator by focusing on the `isGenerating` state. I am updating `bg-amber-500 animate-pulse` for the active indicator. I am also implementing subtle visual tweaks to the active status indicator to ensure it clearly communicates the application\'s activity. The UI is adjusted for both light and dark modes. I\'m updating the status card classes.\n\n\n\n**Refining Visual Consistency**\n\nI\'m now refining the visual consistency of the application. I am updating the background colors for light and dark modes to ensure a cohesive look. Specifically, I\'m working with background, border, text, and badge colors for a coherent aesthetic. I\'m focusing on the left and right panels, and their respective headers, ensuring all elements maintain visual harmony, including the markscheme criteria. The footer color and text are being updated as well. Finally, I\'m integrating colors for \"Score: Optimal\" and the markscheme criteria box.\n\n\n\n**Executing Code Adjustments**\n\nI\'m now executing adjustments to the codebase, beginning with `index.css`. I\'m incorporating the font and custom dark variant, ensuring correct implementation.  Next, I\'ll update `App.tsx` to handle dark mode state and all necessary visual updates. Finally, I will check the `PDFGenerator.tsx` to ensure proper color settings.\n\n\n"
