steps {
  type: CORTEX_STEP_TYPE_USER_INPUT
  status: CORTEX_STEP_STATUS_DONE
  metadata {
    created_at {
      seconds: 1779319872
      nanos: 964343358
    }
    source: CORTEX_STEP_SOURCE_USER_EXPLICIT
  }
  user_input {
    user_response: "The \"Full Lifecycle\" Storage & Management Prompt\nTask: Upgrade my Google Apps Script backend and UI logic to manage a 2-level file directory (Main Folder > Sub-folder) for an IBDP Geography tool.\n\n1. Advanced Storage & Renaming Logic:\n\nInitialization: Create/Locate a Main Folder. Create a Sub-folder for each entry containing three files (Infographic, Questions, Markscheme).\n\nDynamic Renaming (Entry): Provide a function saveEntry(folderName, blobs) that allows the user to define the Sub-folder name at the moment of creation.\n\nPost-Entry Renaming: Provide a function renameEntry(folderId, newName) that updates the folder name in Google Drive. This must also update the internal names of the 3 files inside to match the new folder name (e.g., NewName_Infographic).\n\n2. Safe Deletion Protocol:\n\nBackend Function: Provide a deleteEntry(folderId) function that moves the entire Sub-folder (and its 3 files) to the Trash.\n\nFrontend UX (Safety Gate): I need the logic for a \"Double-Check\" deletion UI.\n\nWhen a user clicks delete, trigger an \'Are you sure?\' modal.\n\nTo confirm, the user must perform a \'Swipe to Delete\' action (simulate this with a slider component or a \'slide-to-confirm\' button) to prevent accidental data loss of exam materials.\n\n3. Technical Constraints:\n\nUse DriveApp for all backend operations.\n\nReturn updated metadata (names and URLs) to the UI after any rename or delete action to keep the dashboard synced.\n\nEnsure the \"Swipe\" logic is written in clean JavaScript/CSS that can be embedded in a standard web app modal.\n\nImplementation Advice for your IBDP App\nSince you are managing specific \"Paper 2\" or \"Unit\" resources, here is how I\342\200\231d handle those new features:\n\nThe \"Swipe to Delete\" Logic\nIn your web app, don\'t just use a standard red button. Use a Range Input (slider) styled to look like a track.\n\nLogic: The deleteEntry function is only called when the slider value reaches 100.\n\nWhy: This mirrors the \"Slide to Power Off\" on iPhones\342\200\224it\342\200\231s the highest level of intentionality for a user, ensuring they don\'t accidentally wipe a calibrated markscheme they spent time refining.\n\nThe Renaming Workflow\nI suggest making the \"Sub-folder\" name the primary \"Key\" in your UI.\n\nDuring Entry: Have a text input field right above your \"Submit New Infographic\" button labeled \"Set Case Study/Topic Name\".\n\nAfter Entry: Add a small \"pencil\" icon next to the generated questions. When clicked, it should turn the text into an input field that triggers your renameEntry script on blur or Enter."
    items {
      text: "The \"Full Lifecycle\" Storage & Management Prompt\nTask: Upgrade my Google Apps Script backend and UI logic to manage a 2-level file directory (Main Folder > Sub-folder) for an IBDP Geography tool.\n\n1. Advanced Storage & Renaming Logic:\n\nInitialization: Create/Locate a Main Folder. Create a Sub-folder for each entry containing three files (Infographic, Questions, Markscheme).\n\nDynamic Renaming (Entry): Provide a function saveEntry(folderName, blobs) that allows the user to define the Sub-folder name at the moment of creation.\n\nPost-Entry Renaming: Provide a function renameEntry(folderId, newName) that updates the folder name in Google Drive. This must also update the internal names of the 3 files inside to match the new folder name (e.g., NewName_Infographic).\n\n2. Safe Deletion Protocol:\n\nBackend Function: Provide a deleteEntry(folderId) function that moves the entire Sub-folder (and its 3 files) to the Trash.\n\nFrontend UX (Safety Gate): I need the logic for a \"Double-Check\" deletion UI.\n\nWhen a user clicks delete, trigger an \'Are you sure?\' modal.\n\nTo confirm, the user must perform a \'Swipe to Delete\' action (simulate this with a slider component or a \'slide-to-confirm\' button) to prevent accidental data loss of exam materials.\n\n3. Technical Constraints:\n\nUse DriveApp for all backend operations.\n\nReturn updated metadata (names and URLs) to the UI after any rename or delete action to keep the dashboard synced.\n\nEnsure the \"Swipe\" logic is written in clean JavaScript/CSS that can be embedded in a standard web app modal.\n\nImplementation Advice for your IBDP App\nSince you are managing specific \"Paper 2\" or \"Unit\" resources, here is how I\342\200\231d handle those new features:\n\nThe \"Swipe to Delete\" Logic\nIn your web app, don\'t just use a standard red button. Use a Range Input (slider) styled to look like a track.\n\nLogic: The deleteEntry function is only called when the slider value reaches 100.\n\nWhy: This mirrors the \"Slide to Power Off\" on iPhones\342\200\224it\342\200\231s the highest level of intentionality for a user, ensuring they don\'t accidentally wipe a calibrated markscheme they spent time refining.\n\nThe Renaming Workflow\nI suggest making the \"Sub-folder\" name the primary \"Key\" in your UI.\n\nDuring Entry: Have a text input field right above your \"Submit New Infographic\" button labeled \"Set Case Study/Topic Name\".\n\nAfter Entry: Add a small \"pencil\" icon next to the generated questions. When clicked, it should turn the text into an input field that triggers your renameEntry script on blur or Enter."
    }
  }
}
