  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering the System Upgrade**\n\nI\'m currently focused on the feasibility of upgrading the Geography infographic generator. My plan is to implement a \"Full Lifecycle\" system within Google Apps Script, leveraging DriveApp for storage and management. I\'m also planning a new UI workflow. I\'m exploring the best approach to integrate these elements seamlessly.\n\n\n**Implementing Folder Structure**\n\nI\'m now focused on the folder structure. I will create a main folder and, for each entry, a sub-folder housing the infographic, questions, and markscheme. I\'ll allow users to name the sub-folder upon creation and provide functionality to update both the folder and file names later. Deletion will be handled by moving the entire sub-folder to the trash, ensuring data integrity.\n\n\n**Refining Implementation Strategy**\n\nI\'ve shifted my focus from Google Apps Script to the Node.js environment I\'m actually working in. I\'ll utilize the Google Drive Node.js SDK with OAuth for backend logic instead of Apps Script. I\'m updating `App.tsx` for entry name input and adding a \"Saved Entries\" view with \"Swipe to Delete\" functionality and renaming logic. My primary goal is now to implement the equivalent logic for the Google Drive API in the Express backend, which is a better fit for this project. I also plan to read up on the `workspace-integration` skill.\n\n\n"
    modified_response: "I will begin by preparing the application for Google Drive integration. This involves reading the workspace integration guidelines and initiating the OAuth setup flow to request the necessary permissions to manage your IBDP Geography folders and files.\n\nNext, I will implement the back-end logic in the server to handle the creation, renaming, and deletion of sub-folders and files according to your specific requirements. This includes the dynamic renaming of internal files to keep your data organized.\n\nFinally, I will update the user interface with a sleek \"Swipe to Delete\" confirmation modal and a topic naming workflow to ensure a professional and secure management experience.\n\n### Skill Check\nI will now read the relevant skill documentation to ensure I follow best practices for Google Workspace integration.\n\nRelevant skills:\n- **workspace-integration** [RELEVANT]\n- **gemini-api** [RELEVANT]\n\n---\n\n### Step 1: Read Workspace Integration Skill\nI need to understand the specifics of implementing Google Drive operations within this environment.\n\n...loading skill: workspace-integration (/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md)\n\n### Step 2: Request OAuth Permissions\nI will request the `https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file` scope. This is safer than full Drive access as it only grants the app permission to access files it creates.\n\n*Note: After I call this tool, I will pause for your confirmation in the UI before proceeding with the implementation.*\n\n---\n\n### Step 3: Implement Folder Logic\nOnce permissions are granted, I will:\n1.  **Initialize**: Create a \"Geo Examiner Records\" folder if it doesn\'t exist.\n2.  **Save Entry**: Modify the upload process to also create a sub-folder and store the three files.\n3.  **Management Routes**: Add Express endpoints for renaming and deleting entries.\n\n---\n\n### Step 4: UI Enhancements\n1.  **Topic Input**: Add a \"Topic Name\" field to the upload section.\n2.  **Swipe to Delete**: Create a custom slider component for the deletion modal.\n3.  **History Panel**: Add a way to view and manage past entries.\n\nLet\'s get started.\n\n<tool_code>\nview_file(AbsolutePath: \"/skills/system_skills/workspace_integration/SKILL.md\", toolAction: \"Reading workspace integration skill\", toolSummary: \"Workspace skill reading\")\nset_up_oauth(requested_scopes: [\"https://www.googleapis.com/auth/drive.file\"], title: \"Use Drive to manage exam materials\", toolAction: \"Initiating OAuth setup for Google Drive integration\", toolSummary: \"OAuth setup\", userConfirmedInUI: false)\n</tool_code>\346\255\242"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 4
      nanos: 239326713
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
