  planner_response {
    thinking: "**Considering File Storage Options**\n\nOkay, I\'m now actively focusing on how to implement this \"on the website\" file storage for the Geography tool. My priority is to move away from Google Drive and find an in-house solution. The system is a full-stack application (Express + Vite), so I\'m considering best practices here. I\'m thinking about storage structure, security, and scalability with this.\n\n\n**Defining the Upload System**\n\nI\'m now designing the file upload system. I\'ll use server-side storage with a local directory for simplicity and persistence, along with a database for metadata. Specifically, I\'ll need a 2-level directory structure (main folder > sub-folder) and functions for saving, renaming, and deleting entries, including handling different file types (PDF, JSON). I\'m also considering the user interface for the frontend, like \"Swipe to Delete\" and renaming UI.\n\n\n**Refining Data Persistence**\n\nI\'m now zeroing in on data persistence. Given the \"on the website\" feel, I initially considered local storage, but I realize this is ephemeral in a containerized environment. Firebase Storage and Firestore are better for persistence. I will likely use Firestore for metadata and Firebase Storage for the actual files, and try to organize files for easy access. I\'ll need to account for a two-level directory structure, as the prompt specifies. I\'m going to start setting up Firebase to handle this correctly.\n\n\n**Implementing API Endpoints**\n\nNow, I\'m working to implement the API endpoints in Express. I\'ll need to handle saving, listing, renaming, and deleting entries within a 2-level directory. The data model in Firestore is taking shape with the \"entries\" collection. For the frontend, I\'m integrating the topic name input, history list (replacing the previous sidebar), and swipe-to-delete. Renaming functionality via a pencil icon is also in development. The constraint check reminds me to stay focused on user-specified features, and I will also implement firebase-integration.\n\n\n"
    thinking_duration {
      seconds: 7
      nanos: 48097558
    }
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
