    modified_response: "I have upgraded the application to include the **Full Lifecycle Storage & Management** system, allowing you to manage exam materials directly on the web server with high intentionality.\n\n### Key Implementation Details:\n\n- **Local Multi-Level Storage**:\n    - Implemented a server-side storage engine using `fs-extra` that creates a structured directory for every entry: `Main Folder > [Entry ID] > (Infographic, Questions, Markscheme)`.\n    - **Dynamic Renaming**: Files are automatically renamed based on the **Topic/Case Study** name (e.g., `Climate_Change_Infographic.jpg`).\n- **Persistence Layer**:\n    - **Firestore Integration**: Used Firebase Firestore to store persistent metadata for all entries, ensuring the dashboard stays synced even after page refreshes.\n    - **Metadata Sync**: Renames and deletions are mirrored both on the physical disk and in the cloud database.\n- **Advanced UX Protocol**:\n    - **Topic Initialization**: Added a mandatory topic naming field before generation to establish the \"Key\" for the new folder.\n    - **Pencil Icon Renaming**: Integrated an \"on-the-fly\" renaming feature in the sidebar. Clicking the pencil icon allows you to update the topic name, which triggers a backend file-renaming sequence across all three assets.\n    - **\"Swipe to Delete\" Safety Gate**: Replaced the standard delete button with a high-intentionality **Draggable Slider**. You must slide the \"Trash\" icon across the track to confirm deletion, preventing accidental loss of calibrated materials.\n- **Resource Lifecycle**:\n    - **Safe Deletion**: Deleting an entry move the files to a `.trash` directory on the server and purges the Firestore record.\n    - **Automated Indexing**: The sidebar history tracks all stored case studies with real-time sync.\n\n### Technical Stack:\n- **Backend**: Node.js/Express with `fs-extra` and `uuid`.\n- **Frontend**: React with `framer-motion` (for the swipe logic) and `lucide-react`.\n- **Database**: Firebase Firestore.\n- **Storage**: Local server disk (serving `/public/uploads` statically)."
    stop_reason: STOP_REASON_STOP_PATTERN
  }
}
